_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Problem\r\n\r\nWhen setting `Normal` highlights for a floating window, the window shows `Pmenu` highlight. I used `git bisect` to see that this started at d879331 (cc @bfredl).\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n```\r\nnvim --clean example.vim\r\n```\r\n\r\nAdd the following code, which opens a floating window and sets its highlighting to `Normal`:\r\n\r\n```vim\r\nlet buf = nvim_create_buf(v:false, v:true)\r\nlet popup = nvim_open_win(buf, 0, {\r\n      \\   'relative':  'editor',\r\n      \\   'row':       15,\r\n      \\   'col':       5,\r\n      \\   'width':     20,\r\n      \\   'height':    5,\r\n      \\   'focusable': v:false,\r\n      \\   'style':     'minimal',\r\n      \\   'border':    'single',\r\n      \\ })\r\ncall setwinvar(popup, '&winhighlight', 'Normal:Normal')\r\n```\r\n\r\nSource the code.\r\n\r\n```\r\n:source %\r\n```\r\n\r\nA floating window with `Pmenu` highlighting appears.\r\n\r\n![actual](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/541289/230238236-4d21cfdc-a646-48e2-a2dc-5f6872794beb.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nA floating window with `Normal` highlighting would appear. Here's an example using an earlier version of Neovim, 0.7.2.\r\n\r\n![expected](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/541289/230238308-5a7d18d2-092d-4996-acc5-4014875abb24.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version (nvim -v)\r\n\r\n0.8.0\r\n\r\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\r\n\r\nNot applicable\r\n\r\n### Operating system/version\r\n\r\nKubuntu 22.10\r\n\r\n### Terminal name/version\r\n\r\nKonsole 22.08.2\r\n\r\n### $TERM environment variable\r\n\r\nxterm-256color\r\n\r\n### Installation\r\n\r\nappimage","closed_by":{"login":"bfredl","id":1363104,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjMxMDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1363104?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfredl","html_url":"https://github.com/bfredl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bf